How to connect Instance putty with Terminal

Steps to connect Instance putty with Terminal
======================================================


with keypair ---------------> it will be present and maintained by AWS cloud
without Keypair ---------------> it will be present and maintained by server what we are going to create


keypair has 2 types

1. PEM keypair (Putty doesn't support this PPK) ----------------> by using with this PEM keypair we can connect easily to any server directly terminal like mobaxterm, 
vscode, command promt, git bash etc but for suppose if we want to connect with PUTTY means first we need to convert this PEM file into a PPK file with that PPK file we can 
connect easily with putty 

2. PPK (PUTTY PRIVATE KEY) keypair (Putty supports only this PPK file)----------------> 

For suppose if we have PEM file means we can't connect with PUTTY it is not possibleprivate key 



Steps to connect Instance putty with Terminal
======================================================

first create a instance pem keypair -------------> for that created instance both have public & private ips ------------> putty support PPK keypair here, we need to 
convert PEM into a PPK file by using puttygen ----------> select puttygen and open it ------------> click on load ---------> select that PEM file click on ok-------->
select save private key -----------> select yes --------> save the file in somwhere like downloads or any other folder with file name as as we wish ---------->
done converted PEM into a PPK file 

Now we can connect PPK file with putty easily -----> copy the public ip of instance ----------> select and open putty ------------> paste the publc ip of the instance
----------> select SSH option and expand it --------------> again select Auth option and expand it ------------> selec credentials option --------------> select an 
option browse select the PPK file select open and accept ---------------> connected with putty successfully ------------> login as given command ec2-user

